    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "import csv\nimport re\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n  return re.findall(r\"\\w+\", text)\n\n\ndef get_frequencies(text):\n  frequencies = {}\n  words = tokenize(text)\n\n  # TODO: Build dictionary\n\n  return frequencies\n\n\ndef main():\n\n  # Read sites\n  f = open(\"recipes.csv\")\n  sites = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n  f.close()\n\n  # Get keyword\n  keyword = input(\"Keyword: \").lower()\n\n  # Search sites\n  highest_frequency = 0\n  best_site = None\n  for site in sites:\n    frequencies = get_frequencies(site[\"content\"])\n    if keyword in frequencies and frequencies[keyword] > highest_frequency:\n      highest_frequency = frequencies[keyword]\n      best_site = site[\"title\"]\n\n  # Print best\n  if best_site:\n    print(f\"Best site: \\\"{best_site}\\\"\")\n  else:\n    print(\"No relevant site.\")\n\n\nmain()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "recipes.csv",
          "contents": "\"title\",\"content\"\n\"Tomato Soup\",\"Tomato soup is a warm, comforting dish made by simmering ripe tomato with onion and garlic until soft. Blend the mixture until smooth, then stir in cream and a pinch of salt. Serve the hot soup with fresh basil on top and a splash of olive oil.\"\n\"Homemade Pizza\",\"To make pizza, stretch the dough into a thin circle and spread a layer of tomato sauce across the top. Sprinkle on shredded cheese and your favorite toppings, then bake in a very hot oven until the crust turns golden and the cheese bubbles. Let it cool for a minute before slicing.\"\n\"Garlic Bread\",\"Garlic bread is a simple side dish made by mixing butter, garlic, and parsley and spreading it on sliced bread. Bake until the edges are crisp and golden. This bread would be a great addition to pizza night, and it also pairs well with pasta. Serve it next to a hot pizza, or bring it to any pizza party.\"\n\"Hosting a Birthday Party\",\"A good birthday party needs food, games, and a plan for the cake. Many hosts order pizza because it is easy to serve and kids love it. Plan on one large pizza for every three guests, plus a plain cheese option for picky eaters. Save room in the fridge for the cake and the drinks.\"\n\"Pizza Dough from Scratch\",\"Mix warm water, yeast, and a spoonful of sugar, then wait until the yeast looks foamy. Stir in flour and salt, and knead the dough for ten minutes until it feels smooth and stretchy. Let the dough rise in a covered bowl for one hour before you shape it.\"\n\"Pepperoni Calzones\",\"A calzone is folded dough filled with cheese and pepperoni and baked until golden. It is like a pizza that you can eat with your hands. Dip each calzone in warm tomato sauce, the same sauce you would spread on a pizza. Cut a small slit in the top so steam can escape.\"\n\"Pizza Coupons: Save on Kitchen Deals\",\"Looking for the best coupon codes? Our site lists discounts on kitchen gadgets, plates, and cooking tools. Sign up for our weekly email to get a new coupon every Monday. Free shipping is available on orders over fifty dollars.\"\n\"Lemon Herb Roast Chicken\",\"A whole roast chicken is the centerpiece of many Sunday dinners. The skin turns crisp and golden while the meat stays juicy, and one bird can feed a family with leftovers for sandwiches. Pat the chicken dry, rub it with butter, lemon zest, salt, and chopped thyme, and tuck a halved lemon inside. Roast it in a hot oven for about an hour and a half, until the juices run clear. Let the bird rest for fifteen minutes before carving so the meat stays moist. Spoon the pan juices over the slices and serve with roasted potatoes.\"\n\"Chicken Noodle Soup\",\"Chicken noodle soup is the food many people ask for when they feel sick, and it has a reputation for helping people feel better. The broth is warm and salty, the noodles are soft, and the vegetables add a little sweetness. Simmer chicken, carrot, celery, and onion in broth until the chicken is tender. Remove the chicken, shred it with two forks, and return it to the pot with egg noodles. Cook until the noodles are soft, then season the soup with salt and pepper. A big pot keeps well, so it makes good leftovers the next day.\"\n\"Chicken Taco Skillet\",\"Busy families love a taco skillet because the whole meal cooks in one pan. Chicken cooked with taco spices is juicy and full of flavor, and everyone can build a plate the way they like it. Cut the chicken into small pieces and brown it in a hot pan with chili powder, cumin, and salt. Add black beans, corn, and a splash of water and simmer for ten minutes. Spoon the mixture into warm tortillas and top with shredded cheese, lettuce, and salsa. Squeeze a little lime over each taco just before eating.\"\n\"Creamy Chicken Pasta\",\"Creamy chicken pasta is a comfort food that turns a plain weeknight into something special. The sauce is rich and smooth, the chicken is tender, and the noodles soak up the flavor. Season sliced chicken with salt and pepper and brown it in a pan, then set it aside. In the same pan, stir cream, a little chicken broth, and grated cheese into a smooth sauce. Boil the pasta until tender, drain it, and toss it with the sauce and the chicken. Sprinkle with parsley and serve right away while the pasta is hot.\"\n\"Chicken Salad Sandwich\",\"Chicken salad is a good way to use up leftover roast chicken, and it makes an easy lunch that needs no cooking. It is creamy, a little crunchy, and it travels well in a lunch box. Chop the chicken into small pieces and stir in mayonnaise, diced celery, and a squeeze of lemon. Season with salt and pepper and spread the salad on soft bread. Add a leaf of lettuce and a slice of tomato before closing the sandwich. Cut it in half and serve it with a handful of grapes.\"\n\"Moroccan Chicken Stew\",\"This stew comes from the kitchens of North Africa, where slow cooking and warm spices are a tradition. The chicken simmers until it falls off the bone in a sauce flavored with cumin, cinnamon, and sweet apricots. It is usually spooned over a bed of fluffy couscous, which soaks up all the sauce. Brown chicken thighs in a heavy pot, then add onion, spices, chickpeas, and broth. Cover the pot and simmer for forty minutes. While the stew cooks, pour hot water over the couscous, cover it, and fluff it with a fork. Serve the stew over the couscous, because the couscous is what makes the meal feel complete.\"\n\"Mashed Potatoes and Gravy\",\"Mashed potatoes with gravy is a side dish that makes a holiday table feel complete. The potatoes are smooth and buttery, and the gravy adds a rich, savory flavor. Boil peeled potatoes in salted water until soft, drain them well, and mash them with butter and warm milk. For the gravy, use the drippings from a roast chicken, whisk in flour, and slowly add chicken broth until the gravy thickens. Season the chicken gravy with pepper, and taste before adding more salt. Serve the potatoes next to roast chicken, and pour the gravy over both the potatoes and the chicken.\"\n\"Garlic Shrimp Scampi Pasta\",\"Scampi is an Italian-American dish of shrimp cooked in butter, lemon, and plenty of garlic. The shrimp cook in just a few minutes, so the whole meal is ready quickly. Melt butter with olive oil in a wide pan and cook minced garlic until fragrant, but do not let it burn. Add the shrimp and cook for two minutes on each side until pink. Squeeze in lemon juice and add chopped parsley. Toss the sauce with hot linguine, and serve the pasta right away with crusty bread.\"\n\"Shrimp Taco Night\",\"Shrimp cooks so fast that it makes a taco dinner possible in twenty minutes. A good shrimp taco is a mix of warm tortilla, spicy shrimp, and cool toppings. Toss peeled shrimp with chili powder, lime juice, and a pinch of salt. Cook the shrimp in a hot pan for two minutes on each side until pink and curled. Warm the tortillas, then pile on shrimp, shredded cabbage, sliced avocado, and a spoonful of creamy sauce. Serve each taco with a lime wedge.\"\n\"Shrimp and Corn Soup\",\"This soup is thick, sweet, and a little spicy, and it tastes like the Gulf Coast. Fresh shrimp and sweet corn are a classic pair, and together they make a soup that works as a full dinner. Cook diced onion and peppers in butter until soft, then add corn and broth. Simmer for fifteen minutes, then stir in cream and a pinch of paprika. Add the shrimp last and cook only until they turn pink, or they will become tough. Serve the soup hot with crackers.\"\n\"Cajun Shrimp and Couscous\",\"This quick dinner pairs spicy shrimp with soft, fluffy couscous. Cajun seasoning gives the shrimp a smoky kick, and the couscous cools it down. Toss the shrimp with paprika, cayenne, garlic powder, and salt, then sear them in a hot skillet until pink. Meanwhile, pour boiling broth over the couscous, cover it, and let it sit for five minutes. Fluff the couscous with a fork and stir in chopped green onion. Serve the shrimp over the couscous with lemon wedges.\"\n\"Coconut Shrimp\",\"Coconut shrimp is a party appetizer with a crisp, golden crust and a hint of sweetness. The shrimp stay juicy on the inside while the coconut toasts on the outside. Set up three bowls for dipping: flour, beaten egg, and a mix of coconut and bread crumbs. Dip each shrimp in order, pressing the coating on gently. Bake the shrimp on a hot tray, turning once, until they turn golden. Serve them with sweet chili sauce for dipping.\"\n\"Beef Taco Tuesday\",\"Many families make tacos on Tuesday, and the habit has become a tradition across the country. A beef taco is simple, filling, and easy to customize. Brown ground beef in a pan with chopped onion and drain off the extra fat. Stir in chili powder, cumin, oregano, and a little water and simmer until the beef is thick. Warm the taco shells in the oven and fill them with the beef. Top with shredded cheese, lettuce, and diced tomato.\"\n\"Fish Taco with Cabbage Slaw\",\"A fish taco has a light, fresh flavor that comes from the mix of crispy fish and crunchy cabbage. This style of taco became popular on the beaches of Baja California. Season white fish with cumin, salt, and lime juice, then pan fry it until it flakes with a fork. For the slaw, toss shredded cabbage with lime juice, cilantro, and a pinch of salt. Warm corn tortillas in a dry pan. Fill each tortilla with a piece of fish and a pile of slaw.\"\n\"Black Bean Taco Bowls\",\"Not every taco needs meat. Black beans are full of protein, and they make a hearty base for a taco bowl. Warm the beans in a pan with cumin, chili powder, and a splash of water until they turn creamy. Cook a pot of rice and stir in lime juice and chopped cilantro. Build each bowl with rice, beans, corn, diced pepper, and shredded lettuce. Top with salsa, avocado, and crushed tortilla chips for crunch.\"\n\"Cilantro Lime Rice\",\"This rice is a simple side dish that goes with almost any Mexican-style dinner. It is fluffy and bright, with a fresh lime flavor. It is the rice most often served on taco night, and it is the perfect base for a taco bowl. Cook long grain rice in water with a pinch of salt until it is tender. Fluff it with a fork and stir in lime juice, lime zest, and a big handful of chopped cilantro. Spoon it next to a taco plate, or pile it into a bowl and top it with taco toppings. Leftover rice can be rolled up in a taco the next day.\"\n\"Taco Seasoning from Scratch\",\"Store bought taco seasoning is full of salt, and the homemade kind takes only a minute to mix. You probably already have everything in your kitchen. Combine chili powder, cumin, paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, oregano, salt, and pepper in a small jar. Shake well. Use two tablespoons for every pound of beef or chicken. The mix keeps for months in a closed jar.\"\n\"Spaghetti and Meatballs\",\"Spaghetti and meatballs is a favorite Italian-American dinner. Soft meatballs in tomato sauce sit on top of a heap of long noodles. Mix ground beef with bread crumbs, an egg, grated cheese, and chopped parsley. Roll the mixture into balls and brown them in a pan. Simmer the meatballs in tomato sauce for twenty minutes. Boil the spaghetti until tender and serve the meatballs and sauce over the top.\"\n\"Baked Pasta Casserole\",\"A baked pasta casserole is made for sharing. The pasta is tender, the sauce is rich, and the cheese on top turns brown and bubbly. Cook the pasta until it is slightly firm, since it softens again in the oven. Mix it with tomato sauce, ricotta, and cooked sausage. Pour everything into a deep dish and cover with shredded mozzarella. Bake until the cheese melts and the edges bubble. Let it rest for ten minutes before serving.\"\n\"Pesto Pasta Salad\",\"Pasta salad is a picnic favorite that tastes good cold. This one uses pesto, a bright green sauce made from basil, nuts, and olive oil. Boil short pasta like rotini or bowtie until tender. Rinse it with cold water so it stops cooking. Toss the pasta with pesto, halved cherry tomato, and cubes of mozzarella. Chill the salad for an hour before serving.\"\n\"Weeknight Pasta with Sausage\",\"This is a fast dinner for nights when there is no time to plan. Italian sausage gives the pasta plenty of flavor with almost no work. Brown crumbled sausage in a large pan with sliced onion. Add a can of crushed tomato and a handful of spinach and simmer for ten minutes. Boil the noodles and toss them with the sauce. Serve with grated cheese.\"\n\"Italian Green Salad\",\"A crisp green salad is the traditional opening for an Italian dinner, served right before the pasta. The salad is light, which keeps the guests hungry for the main course of pasta. Tear romaine and a few leaves of radicchio into a large bowl. Add sliced cucumber, thin red onion, and a handful of olives. Whisk olive oil, red wine vinegar, oregano, and salt for the dressing. Toss the salad just before serving. Pair it with any pasta dish, and set out grated cheese for the pasta.\"\n\"French Onion Soup\",\"French onion soup is a classic from Paris that turns a few plain onions into something rich. The onions are cooked slowly until they turn dark and sweet. Slice six onions and cook them in butter over low heat for forty-five minutes. Add beef broth and a splash of wine, and simmer. Ladle the soup into bowls, top with toasted bread and a thick layer of cheese. Broil until the cheese is brown and bubbly.\"\n\"Lentil Soup\",\"Lentil soup is cheap, hearty, and good for you, and it is eaten in many parts of the world. Lentils cook quickly and need no soaking. Cook diced carrot, celery, and onion in olive oil for five minutes. Add rinsed lentils, broth, cumin, and a bay leaf. Simmer for thirty minutes until the lentils are soft. Squeeze lemon into the pot before serving.\"\n\"Minestrone Soup\",\"Minestrone is an Italian vegetable soup, and the recipe changes with the season. It is a good way to use up the odds and ends in the refrigerator. Cook onion, carrot, and zucchini in olive oil, then add beans, diced tomato, and broth. Simmer until the vegetables are soft. Stir in a handful of small pasta shapes and cook until tender. Serve with grated cheese.\"\n\"Grilled Cheese Sandwich\",\"The grilled cheese sandwich is one of the simplest meals there is, with only bread, butter, and cheese. Even so, a well-made one is crisp on the outside and gooey on the inside. Many people eat it with a bowl of soup, and the sandwich is perfect for dunking. Tomato soup is the classic pairing, but it also goes well with any creamy soup. To make it, spread butter on the outside of two slices of bread and place a few slices of cheese between them. Cook in a pan over medium heat until the bread is golden, then flip and cook until the cheese melts. Cut the sandwich in strips and serve it next to a hot cup of soup.\"\n\"Lemon Herb Couscous\",\"Couscous is a tiny pasta made from wheat that cooks in five minutes, which makes it ideal for a fast side dish. It has a mild flavor, so it picks up whatever seasoning you add. Bring broth to a boil and pour it over the couscous in a bowl. Cover and wait five minutes, then fluff with a fork. Stir in lemon juice, olive oil, chopped parsley, and salt. Serve it warm next to chicken or fish.\"\n\"Mediterranean Couscous Salad\",\"This salad is full of color and works well for picnics. The couscous soaks up the dressing, and the vegetables add crunch. Prepare the couscous with hot water and let it cool. Stir in diced cucumber, cherry tomato, chickpeas, and crumbled feta cheese. Whisk olive oil, lemon juice, and oregano for the dressing. Toss everything together and chill for thirty minutes.\"\n\"Couscous Stuffed Peppers\",\"Stuffed peppers make a pretty dinner, and couscous is an easy filling. The peppers soften in the oven while the filling turns golden on top. Cut the tops off four bell peppers and scoop out the seeds. Mix cooked couscous with sauteed onion, spinach, raisins, and a little cumin. Spoon the filling into the peppers and set them in a baking dish. Bake for thirty minutes.\"\n\"Roasted Vegetable Couscous\",\"Roasting vegetables brings out their sweetness, and couscous makes a soft bed for them. Toss zucchini, red pepper, and red onion with olive oil and salt. Roast on a tray at high heat for twenty-five minutes until the edges brown. Meanwhile, prepare the couscous with boiling broth. Spoon the vegetables over the couscous and top with toasted nuts.\"\n\"Slow Cooker Beef Stew\",\"Beef stew is a one-pot dinner that cooks on its own all day. The beef becomes so tender that it falls apart with a spoon. Brown cubes of beef in a pan, then move them to the slow cooker. Add potato, carrot, onion, broth, and thyme. Cook on low for eight hours. Serve the stew with warm bread.\"\n\"Baked Salmon\",\"Salmon is a rich, flaky fish that bakes in only fifteen minutes. A little seasoning is all it needs. Place the fillets on a tray lined with foil. Rub them with olive oil, salt, pepper, and lemon juice. Bake in a hot oven until the fish flakes easily with a fork. Serve with rice and steamed broccoli.\"\n\"Veggie Burgers\",\"A veggie burger can be as satisfying as a beef burger when it is made with beans and oats. Mash a can of black beans, leaving some chunks. Stir in oats, chopped onion, cumin, and an egg. Shape the mixture into four patties. Cook in a pan until crisp on both sides. Serve on toasted buns with lettuce and sliced tomato.\"",
